/keld
*.test
# Local installer dry-run build output dirs (installers-<os>-<arch>/, e.g. from
# `act`/local CI runs) and the Inno Setup output dir — not the tracked installers/
# source tree itself. An earlier bare `/installers*` pattern here accidentally
# matched that tracked dir too (no untracked files under it could be `git add`ed).
/installers-*/
/installers/windows/Output/

# GoReleaser build output
/dist/

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Local dev install-mirror artifacts (served to the web app for curl|sh testing)
/.dev-dl/

/build
/windows

# Editor/agent state and macOS directory metadata. Neither belongs in the repo, and
# both otherwise leave the working tree permanently "unclean" — which is precisely
# what scripts/cut-release.sh refuses to tag from, so an ignored-but-present
# `.claude/worktrees/` was enough to block every release from this checkout.
# Scoped rather than a bare `/.claude/`: a shared `.claude/settings.json` is
# something a team may well want tracked, and this must not foreclose that.
.DS_Store
/.claude/settings.local.json
/.claude/worktrees/

# Rust build output for the desktop shell (app/src-tauri). 2.9 GB of
# artifacts; the .app bundle is a BUILD PRODUCT, rebuilt by
#   cd app && npx @tauri-apps/cli build --bundles app
# An earlier commit added 3,286 of these files by accident.
/app/src-tauri/target/

# Tauri build output: tauri_build rewrites these on every build (Tauri's own
# app template ignores them too). 4,714 lines were committed by accident.
/app/src-tauri/gen/schemas
